Step 1: Patient Eligibility & Intake
Real-World Alignment: High. Many administrative delays are caused by submitting prior authorizations (PAs) for active plans that do not actually require authorization for the specific CPT/HCPCS code, or for plans that have been terminated.
Educational Value: Explaining the role of the electronic Benefit Verification (eBV) system correctly teaches users that eligibility and code checks must precede the labor-intensive clinical compilation phase.
Step 2: Medical Necessity Evaluation (Guideline Matching)
Real-World Alignment: Exceptional. Utilization Review (UR) clinicians do not simply answer multiple-choice questions; they actively abstract objective indicators from EHR clinical narratives to satisfy structured guidelines like Milliman Care Guidelines (MCG) or InterQual.
Scenario Integrity:
Total Hip Arthroplasty: Accurately identifies the need to prove the failure of conservative management (physical therapy, NSAIDs) and objective radiological proof of joint-space narrowing.
Lumbar MRI: Correctly teaches the "red flag" exception rules. Uncomplicated lower back pain typically requires 6 weeks of conservative therapy before advanced imaging is authorized. However, progressive neurological deficits—such as foot drop—allow clinicians to override this timeframe immediately.
